<section>

    <section id="test12">
        <h2>Does text have sufficient contrast? </h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Text smaller than 24px: minimum 4,5:1</li>
            <li>Text larger than 24px: minimum 3:1</li>
            <li>Bold text of 18,5px and more: minimum 3:1</li>
        </ul>

    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Tool : Color contrast analyser</h2>
        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/pensioen_color_contrast_analyser.png" alt="screenshot of color contrast analyser"></p>

    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Tool : Firefox accessibility inpector tool</h2>
        <p>Press F12, then select the accessibility tab, then look for contrast problems or inspect elements manually</p>

        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/Firefox_contrast_dev_tools_fr.png" alt="looking for contrast issues with Firefox dev tools"></p>
        <p>Works for texts on background images. </p>

    </section>



    <section>
        <h2>Tool : Chrome dev tools</h2>
        <p>Press F12, then select inspector <img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/chrome_devtools_inspector_button.jpg" alt=""></p>
        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/chrome_devtools_contrast.jpg" alt="Chrome devtools inspector showing contrast ratio of text"></p>

    </section>

    <section id="test13">
        <h2>Do non text elements have enough contrast? </h2>
        <p>minimum 3:1 for </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Icons</li>
            <li>Form fields</li>
            <li>States (focus, hover, ...)</li>
            <li>Parts of a diagram</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Icons</h2>
        <p>Does shape of icon have enough contrast with adjacent colors? </p>
        <img class="stretch" src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/Contraste_ex1.png" alt="Several icons with different contrasts">
        <p>It only matters for icons that convey information!</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Form fields</h2>
        <p>Can you see identify the form field well enough ? Is there a contrast of 3 between form field and adjacent colors ? </p>
        <p><a href="https://codepen.io/sophieschuermans/full/gOQVXGV">Exercice : Check outline of text field, radio button and checkboxes. </a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Focus indicator</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Does focus indicator have enough contrast with adjacent colors ? </li>
            <li>Is there enough contrast between focused and non focused state? </li>   
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Focus indicator - example of insufficient contrast</h2>
        <p>Same button without focus and with focus : </p>
        <img  src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/BNP_green_button.png" alt="Green button" >
        <img  src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/BNP_green_button_focus.png" alt="same green button, a bit darker, with light green outline" >
        <ul>
            <li>Contrast between initial and focus button color is &lt; 3  </li>
            <li>Contrast between light green outline and adjacent white is &lt; 3</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Focus indicator - example of sufficient contrast</h2>
        <p>Same button without focus and with focus : </p>
        <img  src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/BNP_green_button.png" alt="Green button" >
        <img  src="https://images.anysurfer.be/contrast/BNP_green_button_focus_darkoffset.png" alt="same green button, a bit darker, with light green and dark green outline" >
        <ul>
            <li>Contrast between initial and focus button color is &lt; 3  </li>
            <li>Contrast between dark green outline and adjacent white is > 3</li>
        </ul>
    </section>


    <section>
        <h2>Focus indicator - exercice</h2>
        <p><a href="https://codepen.io/sophieschuermans/full/MWzNEvW">Check contrast of focus indicators on links and buttons</a></p>
    </section>
</section>
